@meeting careerChief
// PLACEHOLDER (the career engineer, 0.61.0): head writer 4 writes the real one. The Chief's talking-to: your work
// standing has fallen low (missed shifts without leave). An appointment in the Chief's office, Deck 5, the next
// workday morning. Plays when you're in the room; missed, the gist comes by Mail.
title: A word with the Chief
from: Chief Ines Calder
gist: You didn't come to the Chief's office. Calder says the talk will keep, and so will the record.
== lines
calder > you: Shut the door. Sit.   [gesture]
calder: You've missed shifts. No leave booked, no word to anyone. The board noticed before I did.
calder: Everyone has bad weeks. If you need a day, book it on your device. That's what leave is for.
? choice
* It won't happen again, Chief.   rel:calder+1
  calder: Good. Eight o'clock, Works bay. I'll see you there.
* I've been struggling a bit.   rel:calder+2
  calder: Then say so. Talk to Rina, or to me. But turn up.   [nod]
* (Say nothing)
  calder: Silence I can work with. Absence I can't.
calder: Turn up, do the jobs, and this goes away. That's all.
